  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Read the results as synthetic",
      "items": [
        "All 15,000 saved alumni records are invented fixtures; skills are course exposure tags, not measured proficiency.",
        "Only entry and year-three jobs are observed. Years six and nine are absorbing-chain scenarios.",
        "O*NET provides national posting shares and tasks; there is no scraped job-postings dataset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Preparation and execution",
      "items": [
        "Reference preparation groups the existing course CSV, curated skill exporter and onet_skills.py. Alumni generation also reads companies.json.",
        "run_all.py launches seven scripts in order and stops if one fails. Only market-demand building must precede gap_matrix.py.",
        "Salary models read company_tiers.csv; the RPP specification runs only when the cost-of-living template is complete."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Independent PDF branch and file map",
      "items": [
        "Eight career-guide PDFs \u2192 parsing_json_pdf.py \u2192 per-major JSON + all_career_outcomes.json. These outputs are not read by the current analyses.",
        "The companion project-files.html maps source folders, scripts, generated artifacts and generator tests.",
        "Chart rendering reads saved tables without refitting models; it imports an installed chart-style helper and requires suitable fonts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence scope",
      "items": [
        "Based on local project files inspected on 21 October 2026. This project folder is unversioned; source-snapshot/ freezes only the cited files for reproducible documentation.",
        "Source ranges are pinned to the local documentation snapshot, not to the unrelated parent Git repository.",
        "Overview groups preparation and shared execution roles; the file map gives the module-level breakdown."
      ]
    }
  ]
